@title dispatch-jobs queue backlog
@subtitle On-call runbook for Quickpost Couriers
@author Dispatch Engineering, Owner

kpi Alert | > 5,000 | for 10 min (QUEUE_DEPTH_HIGH)
kpi Normal depth | < 400 | messages
kpi Max consumers | 40 | DB pool cap: 200 connections
kpi Escalate after | 20 min | still > 5,000

!!! Never purge `dispatch-jobs`. Every message is a real customer delivery.

# Symptoms
- The `QUEUE_DEPTH_HIGH` alert fires when depth stays above 5,000 for 10 min. Normal is under 400.
- Drivers see new jobs arrive late in the app.

# Diagnose
- Check queue depth and consumer count: `kubectl -n dispatch get hpa dispatch-consumer`
- Look at the oldest message age on the queue dashboard.
- Check the database connection pool, which is capped at 200 connections.

# Fix steps
1. Scale the consumers
-- 1. Run `kubectl -n dispatch scale deploy dispatch-consumer --replicas=24`
-- 2. Wait 5 min and re-check the depth
-- 3. If depth is still rising, scale to 40. This is the maximum the database pool supports; do not go higher.
2. Check for poison messages
-- 1. Look for any message retried more than 10 times
-- 2. Move it to `dispatch-dlq` with the `dlq-move` tool
3. Pause the bulk import scheduler in the admin console. Bulk imports add up to 3,000 jobs at a time.
4. When depth drops under 400, re-enable the scheduler gradually.

!! Do not purge the queue to clear the backlog. Move single poison messages to `dispatch-dlq` instead.

# Escalation
If depth is still above 5,000 after 20 min:
- Page the Dispatch Engineering lead.
- Open an incident in #incidents.
